1104 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This analysis utilizes the Prozhito database\054 a large\055scale corpus of digitized diaries from the Russian Empire through modern Russia\056\nExtraction\056 Regular expressions were utilized to isolate records connected to the feeling of heat\054 filtering out literal descriptions \050of weather or physical illness\056\nAnnotation\056 This targeted filtering produced a concentrated dataset of 301 records\056 Each record was manually annotated using a custom taxonomy\072\nLinguistic Form \050e\056g\056\054 poetic metaphor\054 somatic reaction\054 idiom\051\nEmotional State \050e\056g\056\054 love\054 anxiety\054 excitement\054 anger\054 shame\051\nContext \050e\056g\056\054 politics\054 religion\054 creation\054 interpersonal\051\nData Distribution\056 The final annotated dataset comprises 210 relevant records\056 The chronological distribution is uneven\054 containing 32 records from the XIX century\054 91 from 1899\0231938\054 36 from 1939\0231947\054 24 from 1948\0231979\054 and 27 from 1980\0232017\056 This temporal imbalance reflects the heterogeneous nature of \050the underlying Prozhito database\056)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 1105 0 R
     /Pg 1092 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

